  Read: a tight SPREAD (esp. of the ALL row) at a given burst means the
  fidelity estimate is stable there. If b=0 swings widely but the burst
  columns are tight and high, the raw stale layout is the noisy regime and
  a small burst both raises AND stabilizes decision fidelity.
